      "type": "answer",
      "text": "Based on the repository analysis, here are three priority review items identified from the medium-severity findings:\n\n### 1. `apps/memforks-chat/src/components/chat-app.tsx` (Line 100 & 170)\n*   **Issue:** Missing fetch deadline/timeout.\n*   **Priority:** High (potential for stalled UI/service operations).\n*   **Suggested Fix:** Implement an `AbortSignal` for these fetch calls. You can use `AbortSignal.timeout(ms)` to provide a hard deadline or pass a signal from a controller that allows the component to cancel the request upon unmounting. This prevents a stalled service from holding the application state indefinitely.\n\n### 2. `apps/memforks-chat/src/components/diff-panel.tsx` (Line 40)\n*   **Issue:** Missing fetch deadline/timeout.\n*   **Priority:** Medium.\n*   **Suggested Fix:** Similar to the chat app, ensure the fetch call includes an `AbortSignal`. This ensures that if the diff generation service hangs, the UI can recover or time out rather than remaining in a loading state.\n\n### 3. `packages/cli/scripts/bundle-ui.mjs` (Line 27)\n*   **Issue:** Potentially unsafe shell execution.\n*   **Priority:** Medium (security/robustness).\n*   **Suggested Fix:** Review how commands are being executed. Instead of using generic shell execution methods (like `child_process.exec`) which can be vulnerable to command injection if any part of the command is dynamically constructed, prefer `child_process.execFile`. This allows you to pass a fixed executable and an array of arguments, minimizing the risk of malicious interpolation.",
